    Bug 2001632 - Treat parts with a content-id as attachments only if they also have a name. r=mkmelin


    Usually the presence of a content-id header indicates that a part is an inline element
    referenced from elsewhere in the message as a related part. The current implementation
    however treats those parts as attachments, which should only happen if the part has a
    name.

    This patch modified two tests, which locked down wrong behavior. They both work
    on the same test message:

    https://searchfox.org/comm-central/source/mail/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/messages/invite.eml

    This message has a multipart/related part with the following sub-part:

    ```
    --=_related_36138BFC6A7B03EFC2258776003DB5C5_=↩
    Content-Type: text/html; charset=windows-1257↩
    Content-Disposition: inline↩
    Content-ID: <FFFF__=4DBB0DE5DFAE33558f9e8a93df938690918c4DB@>↩
    ↩
    <html>↩
     <body>↩
      <p>You have been invited to a meeting (RELATED)</p>↩
     </body>↩
    </html>↩
    ↩
    --=_related_36138BFC6A7B03EFC2258776003DB5C5_=--
    ```

    This part is specified as `inline` and has no name. The former implementation
    treated it as an attachment, excluded it's body from `getFull()`, which was wrong.

    This patch does not create a regression for bug 1737532 (whose test is changed).
    All parts are still returned, either as attachments or as inline text parts.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D273796

diff --git a/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionMessages.sys.mjs b/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionMessages.sys.mjs
index 57726fe394f..fccea0f104c 100644
--- a/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionMessages.sys.mjs
+++ b/mail/components/extensions/ExtensionMessages.sys.mjs
@@ -326,8 +326,8 @@ class WebExtMimeTreeEmitter extends MimeTreeEmitter {
       return name;
     }

-    // Handle related attachments.
-    if (mimeTreePart.headers._rawHeaders.has("content-id")) {
+    // Handle related attachments, but skip if they do not have a name.
+    if (name && mimeTreePart.headers._rawHeaders.has("content-id")) {
       return name;
     }

